---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url";

const gates = [
  ["Source gate", "Can the input be identified, versioned, and traced to an allowed source?"],
  ["Quality gate", "Does the evidence meet the declared completeness and quality threshold?"],
  ["Uncertainty gate", "Is confidence calibrated enough for this decision, or should the system abstain?"],
  ["Approval gate", "Does the proposed action require explicit human review before it can proceed?"],
];
---
<Base title="Approach — SciencesLoop" description="How SciencesLoop structures evidence-gated scientific workflows around claims, provenance, uncertainty, abstention, and human approval." alternatePath={u("/zh/approach/")}>
  <div class="sl-page">
    <section class="sl-page-hero"><span class="sl-chip proposed">Product architecture · proposed</span><h1>Make every scientific decision answerable.</h1><p class="sl-lead">The core unit is not an AI response. It is an evidence contract: a claim, the evidence required to support it, a decision rule, and a replayable record of what happened.</p></section>

    <section class="sl-section sl-dark"><div class="sl-section-head"><span>01 · Evidence contract</span><h2>Claim → evidence → gate → decision.</h2></div><div class="sl-trace"><div><b>C</b><strong>Claim</strong><small>Define the question and allowable conclusion</small></div><i>→</i><div><b>E</b><strong>Evidence</strong><small>Bind data, source, version, and transformation</small></div><i>→</i><div><b>G</b><strong>Gate</strong><small>Evaluate quality, uncertainty, and policy</small></div><i>→</i><div><b>D</b><strong>Decision</strong><small>Pass, abstain, or request review</small></div></div></section>

    <section class="sl-section"><div class="sl-section-head"><span>02 · Four gates</span><h2>Reliability comes from explicit stopping rules.</h2></div><div class="sl-grid two">{gates.map(([name, text], i) => <article class="sl-card"><span class="sl-index">0{i + 1}</span><h3>{name}</h3><p>{text}</p></article>)}</div></section>

    <section class="sl-section"><div class="sl-section-head"><span>03 · Evidence states</span><h2>A workflow should say what it knows.</h2></div><div class="sl-state-table" role="table" aria-label="Evidence states"><div role="row"><strong role="columnheader">State</strong><strong role="columnheader">Meaning</strong><strong role="columnheader">Allowed behavior</strong></div><div role="row"><span><i class="state ok"></i>Supported</span><span>Required evidence is present and passes checks.</span><span>Return a bounded result with provenance.</span></div><div role="row"><span><i class="state warn"></i>Conditional</span><span>Evidence is usable but uncertainty or assumptions matter.</span><span>Expose limits and request review when needed.</span></div><div role="row"><span><i class="state stop"></i>Unsupported</span><span>A required source, field, or quality threshold is missing.</span><span>Abstain; do not invent a conclusion.</span></div></div></section>

    <section class="sl-section sl-note"><div><span class="sl-chip working">Working prototype</span><h2>What exists today</h2><p>Public SciencesLoop demos implement bounded pieces of this pattern: deterministic replay, source-linked identity checks, explicit evidence gaps, and human confirmation.</p></div><div><span class="sl-chip proposed">Proposed</span><h2>What comes next</h2><p>A unified scientific workflow layer connecting offline instrument exports, analysis, uncertainty, provenance, and approval. This architecture is not yet a validated production system.</p></div></section>

    <section class="sl-section sl-contact"><div><h2>Inspect the claims, not the pitch.</h2><p>The evidence page separates demonstrated behavior from proposed product direction.</p></div><a class="sl-button primary" href={u("/evidence/")}>Open evidence register</a></section>
  </div>
</Base>
